module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// A cast the compiler refuses although it admits every step of it, filed from a measurement rather than
// inferred. Census run 41768647568 holds the refusals; the admitting legs are pinned by code that
// compiles on main, quoted with their file:line in the receipts. The repair is a compiler-side verdict,
// named in the last receipt, and is not the change that files this row.
data a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "**A TWO-LEG CAST IS REFUSED AS A COMPOSITE ALTHOUGH THE COMPILER ADMITS EACH LEG, AND THE REFUSAL NAMES THE LEG THAT IS ADMITTED** (INVALID STATE: `text as Secret` is admitted, where Secret is a nominal_opaque whose carrier is String; `branded_text as String` is admitted, eliminating a brand to its carrier; `branded_text as Secret` - the composition of exactly those two - refuses at the emit stage, and the diagnostic it prints names the intermediate pair, NonEmptyStr to String, which is one of the legs already admitted. v1.compiler.emit cast_realization_refusal_fact, src/v1/05_emit.dag:3517, builds that text from whatever pair the walk stalled on, so the sentence indicts a crossing that compiles elsewhere in the same corpus).",
    "HARM. The answer cannot be derived from the corpus's own precedents, and it points the reader at the wrong half of the path. Read literally it says the text is unreachable, which invites the reader to carry a SECOND representation of the value beside the branded one so a site has something to cast - two sources for one value, drifting the moment either is written on its own, and the brand stops being the thing identity is taken from. That is the repair this row forbids: it was nearly taken here, on five sites in two modules, and review 90521 on gunbc#15775 stopped it before it landed.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is not the ungrounded-cast class, where an unidentified source or a type variable reaches no verdict at all: here both endpoints are named, both legs are decided, and only the composite is refused. It is also not a missing route: the route exists at std.types.secret_of_text, and taking it is what the sites now do - secret_of_text(jwt as String), an admitted elimination followed by a named entry, with no chained `as` into a nominal (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed names chaining past a refusal as the workaround tell, and the two-hop jwt as String as Secret was proposed and rejected on exactly that ground). The recognition rule is a question to ask of any such refusal, before routing around it: does the pair the diagnostic names appear, admitted, anywhere else in the corpus? Here the answer is yes, three times over, in code that compiles today.",
    "WHAT IS ADMITTED, WITH ITS RECEIPTS. String onto Secret: dag/extdeps/shell/credentials.dag:30 does text as Secret in env_credential_token, on a live chain through gunbc.org_actions_inspection and extdeps.github.auth, and the population that `as` still lets through is counted here, once, with its method: at head a3621c35907 the spelling ' as Secret' occurs 140 times in .dag under dag/, excluding comment lines and excluding this directory's own prose (grep -rn ' as Secret' --include=*.dag dag/, less lines whose first non-space token is //, less dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/). Of those, 60 sit in production modules across 44 files and 80 in dag/test claims. Counted without the exclusions the whole tree gives 153 raw occurrences, which is why the exclusions are part of the number. Branded text onto String: dag/test/claim/github_effect_perform_witness.dag:51 compares a JwtCompactSerialization - dag/extdeps/auth/jws.dag:108, a NonEmptyStr carrying a brand - with `as String`, and extdeps.auth.jws.jws_compact_serialization does signing_input as String on a plain NonEmptyStr, and the witness at :114 does it to EncodedJitConfig.encoded, declared encoded: NonEmptyStr at dag/extdeps/github/actions_jit_runner.dag:68. All three compile on main.",
    "WHAT WAS REFUSED, WITH ITS RECEIPT (2026-11-04, clever-carp-493, census run 41768647568). Five `jwt as Secret` crossings, named by the symbol that holds each: gunbc.github_effect_perform mint_controller_installation_token, publisher_jwt_after_removal and publisher_jwt_from_signed, and gunbc.auth.github_app_control_plane_observe observe_github_app_control_plane at two of its argument positions. Each printed 'cast cannot be emitted for target rust -- no declared conversion route from NonEmptyStr to String'. The positions the census printed - 239:26, 658:65 and 688:63 in the first module, 168:120 and 180:119 in the second - are addresses inside those five symbols as the corpus stood at that head, and they move the moment the crossings do, which is why the symbols carry the citation. The census head is the mirror CI head; it cannot be re-run at main's head until the drift-route PR lands, because main's committed drift-watch step dies at an unrelated TypeError before the emit stage.",
    "THE ROUTE, AND THE ONE ROUTE IT IS HEADED FOR. std.types.secret_of_text is the declared crossing onto Secret, and it is the destination rather than a second path: entering a nominal is a change of interpretation, so gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate requires it to be named at the call site whatever else the compiler lets through. What stands beside it is the compiler's own unevenness - `text as Secret` admitted while the refined alias to the same carrier is refused - and the surviving `as Secret` spellings are that unevenness's debt, which is why they are counted above instead of quietly kept. MIGRATION TRIGGER: migrate every surviving `as Secret` spelling to secret_of_text, all 140 occurrences counted above - the 60 in production modules across 44 files and the 80 in claims, env_credential_token in extdeps.shell.credentials among them, AND tighten the cast rule at the one home for that judgement, v1.compiler.infer grounded_cast_verdict (src/v1/04_infer.dag:8295), so `as` stops admitting an entry into a nominal. Both together retire this row and leave secret_of_text as the only spelling; a migration alone leaves the fork standing, and a tightening alone strands every site the count above covers. No control here goes red when the composite regrows, which is why the rung is stated as unread rather than claimed: this filing changes what five sites write and what the reader is told, and executes nothing.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.types", decl_name: "secret_of_text", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.auth.jws", decl_name: "jws_compact_serialization", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.github_effect_perform", decl_name: "JitMintAppJwt", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "grounded_cast_verdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit", decl_name: "cast_realization_refusal_fact", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
